1
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:03,000
A district attorney out for a conviction. A new lawyer out of
her league. A young boy who knew too much.

2
00:11:54,000 --> 00:12:00,000
The Client is a drama, thriller, crime film directed by Joel Schumacher.

3
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:57,000
A street-wise kid, Mark Sway, sees the suicide of Jerome Clifford, a prominent Louisiana
lawyer, whose current client is Barry 'The Blade' Muldano, a Mafia hit-man.

4
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Before Jerome shoots himself, he tells Mark where
the body of a Senator is buried.

5
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Clifford shoots himself and Mark is found at the scene, and both the FBI and the
Mafia quickly realize that Mark probably knows more than he says.

6
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Mark Sway, played by Brad Renfro.

7
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:45,000
Reggie Love, played by Susan Sarandon.

8
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:42,000
Roy Foltrigg, played by Tommy Lee Jones.

9
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:39,000
Dianne Sway, played by Mary-Louise Parker.

10
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
Barry Muldano, played by Anthony LaPaglia.

11
01:05:27,000 --> 01:05:33,000
Thomas Fink, played by Bradley Whitford.

12
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
The Client is a 1994 American legal thriller film directed by Joel Schumacher, and starring Susan Sarandon, Tommy Lee Jones,
Mary-Louise Parker, Anthony LaPaglia, Anthony Edwards, Ossie Davis, and introducing Brad Renfro in his film debut.

13
01:17:21,000 --> 01:17:27,000
It is based on the 1993 novel by John Grisham.

14
01:23:18,000 --> 01:23:24,000
It was filmed in Memphis, Tennessee.

15
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
The Client was theatrically released in the United States by Warner Bros.

16
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
on July 20, 1994, and was a box-office hit, grossing
$117.6 million against a $45 million budget.

17
01:41:09,000 --> 01:41:15,000
It received positive reviews from critics, with the performances of
Sarandon, Jones and Renfro in particular earning high praise.

18
01:47:06,000 --> 01:47:12,000
The film explores themes of suicide, sibling
relationship, brother, gangster, investigation.

19
01:53:03,000 --> 01:53:09,000
The tone is mind_bending and emotional and intense.
